# The Gradle wrapper is TRACKED, deliberately.
#
# gradle-wrapper.properties pins gradle-9.1.0-all.zip, but gradlew and
# gradle-wrapper.jar are what EXECUTE that pin. A pinned version nobody can run
# is documentation, not reproducibility, so all three are committed together.
#
# The jar is byte-identical to the artifact in the pinned Flutter SDK
# (3.44.9), sha256 16caeaf66d57a0d1d2087fef6a97efa62de8da69afa5b908f40db35afc4342da.
# The supply-chain risk with a committed wrapper jar is not its presence, it is
# that it changes silently: verify that hash before accepting any diff to it.
#
# Tracking them also closes a hygiene trap seen on 2026-08-13. These rules live
# inside the directory they govern, so when apps/ left the working tree on a
# branch switch, android/.gitignore went with it and files that HAD been
# correctly ignored became orphaned untracked debris at paths a later checkout
# would want. A per-directory .gitignore protects a file only while its branch
# is checked out; a tracked file needs no such protection.

/.gradle
/captures/
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
